        <li><LocalizedText sk="vytvárať objekty pomocou __init__ a pracovať s atribútmi a metódami;" en="create objects with __init__ and work with attributes and methods;" /></li>
        <li><LocalizedText sk="vysvetliť, ako objekty spolupracujú;" en="explain how objects collaborate;" /></li>
        <li><LocalizedText sk="používať dedičnosť, prepisovanie metód a super();" en="use inheritance, method overriding and super();" /></li>
        <li><LocalizedText sk="rozhodnúť sa medzi vzťahom is-a a has-a a vyhnúť sa častým chybám návrhu." en="choose between is-a and has-a relationships and avoid common design mistakes." /></li>
      </ul>
    </aside>

    <nav class="oop-toc" aria-label="Obsah témy">
      <strong><LocalizedText sk="Obsah" en="On this page" /></strong>
      <a href="#class-object">1. <LocalizedText sk="Trieda a objekt" en="Class and object" /></a>
      <a href="#state-behavior">2. <LocalizedText sk="Stav a správanie" en="State and behavior" /></a>
      <a href="#constructor">3. <code>__init__</code></a>
      <a href="#attributes">4. <LocalizedText sk="Atribúty" en="Attributes" /></a>
      <a href="#methods">5. <LocalizedText sk="Metódy" en="Methods" /></a>
      <a href="#interaction">6. <LocalizedText sk="Interakcia objektov" en="Object interaction" /></a>
      <a href="#inheritance">7. <LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť a super()" en="Inheritance and super()" /></a>
      <a href="#composition">8. <LocalizedText sk="Kompozícia" en="Composition" /></a>
      <a href="#design-mistakes">9. <LocalizedText sk="Chyby návrhu" en="Design mistakes" /></a>
      <a href="#practice">10. <LocalizedText sk="Precvičenie" en="Practice" /></a>
    </nav>

    <section class="oop-section" id="class-object">
      <h2>1. <LocalizedText sk="Trieda a objekt" en="Class and object" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Trieda (class) je definícia, ktorá opisuje, aké údaje a operácie budú mať objekty daného typu. Objekt (inštancia) je konkrétna vytvorená hodnota tejto triedy. Z jednej triedy môže vzniknúť ľubovoľný počet samostatných objektov." en="A class is a definition that describes the data and operations objects of that type have. An object (instance) is a particular value created from that class. One class can produce any number of separate objects." /></p>

      <div class="oop-concept-grid">
        <article class="oop-concept-card">
          <h3><LocalizedText sk="Trieda = plán" en="Class = blueprint" /></h3>
          <p><LocalizedText sk="Určuje spoločnú štruktúru a správanie. Napríklad trieda Student opisuje, aké údaje a operácie má študent." en="Defines shared structure and behavior. For example, Student describes the data and operations a student has." /></p>
        </article>
        <article class="oop-concept-card">
          <h3><LocalizedText sk="Objekt = konkrétny kus" en="Object = concrete instance" /></h3>
          <p><LocalizedText sk="Je vytvorený podľa triedy a obsahuje konkrétne hodnoty, napríklad študenta s menom Anna a ID B123." en="Is created from the class and contains concrete values, such as a student named Anna with ID B123." /></p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="oop-diagram" role="group" aria-label="Class and instance relationship">
        <div class="oop-diagram-node oop-diagram-class">
          <strong><LocalizedText sk="Trieda Student" en="Class Student" /></strong>
          <span>name: str</span>
          <span>student_id: str</span>
          <span>introduce()</span>
        </div>
        <div class="oop-diagram-connector"><span>↓ <LocalizedText sk="vytvorí" en="creates" /> ↓</span></div>
        <div class="oop-diagram-instances">
          <div class="oop-diagram-node"><strong>student_a</strong><span>Anna · B123</span></div>
          <div class="oop-diagram-node"><strong>student_b</strong><span>Peter · B124</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Student:
    pass


student_a = Student()
student_b = Student()

print(type(student_a).__name__)
print(student_a is student_b)`} />
      <div class="oop-output">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong>
        <pre>Student
False</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Oba objekty vznikli z rovnakej triedy, ale sú to dve rozdielne inštancie. Zatiaľ nemajú vlastné údaje — tie pridáme v ďalších krokoch." en="Both objects were created from the same class, but they are two different instances. They do not have their own data yet — we will add it in the next steps." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="state-behavior">
      <h2>2. <LocalizedText sk="Stav a správanie objektu" en="Object state and behavior" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Objekt spája stav a správanie. Stav tvoria aktuálne hodnoty jeho atribútov. Správanie predstavujú operácie, ktoré objekt dokáže vykonať — v Pythone ich zapisujeme ako metódy." en="An object combines state and behavior. State consists of the current values of its attributes. Behavior is the set of operations the object can perform — in Python, we write these as methods." /></p>
      <div class="oop-comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="oop-comparison-table">
          <thead><tr><th><LocalizedText sk="Časť objektu" en="Object part" /></th><th><LocalizedText sk="Význam" en="Meaning" /></th><th><LocalizedText sk="Príklad" en="Example" /></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong><LocalizedText sk="Stav" en="State" /></strong></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Čo si objekt pamätá." en="What the object remembers." /></td><td><code>balance = 100</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong><LocalizedText sk="Správanie" en="Behavior" /></strong></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Čo objekt dokáže urobiť." en="What the object can do." /></td><td><code>deposit(50)</code></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class BankAccount:
    def __init__(self, owner: str, balance: float = 0) -> None:
        self.owner = owner
        self.balance = balance

    def deposit(self, amount: float) -> None:
        if amount <= 0:
            raise ValueError("Amount must be positive")
        self.balance += amount


account = BankAccount("Anna", 100)
account.deposit(50)
print(account.owner)
print(account.balance)`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>Anna
150</pre></div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Po zavolaní deposit() sa zmenil stav objektu — hodnota balance sa zvýšila zo 100 na 150. Metóda pracovala s údajmi konkrétneho účtu." en="After calling deposit(), the object's state changed — balance increased from 100 to 150. The method worked with the data of that particular account." /></p>
      <div class="oop-mini-example">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Krátke overenie" en="Quick check" /></strong>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Ak má objekt Car atribút speed a metódu accelerate(), čo je stav a čo správanie?" en="If a Car object has an attribute speed and a method accelerate(), which is state and which is behavior?" /></p>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Odpoveď: speed je stav; accelerate() je správanie." en="Answer: speed is state; accelerate() is behavior." /></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="constructor">
      <h2>3. <LocalizedText sk="Konštruktor a inicializácia: __init__" en="Constructor and initialization: __init__" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Pri vytváraní objektu Python najprv pripraví novú inštanciu a následne zavolá metódu __init__ na nastavenie jej počiatočného stavu. V bežnej výučbe sa __init__ často nazýva konštruktor, presnejšie však ide o inicializačnú metódu. Parameter self odkazuje na práve vytváranú inštanciu." en="When an object is created, Python first creates a new instance and then calls __init__ to set its initial state. In introductory teaching, __init__ is often called the constructor; more precisely, it is the initializer. The self parameter refers to the instance being initialized." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class User:
    def __init__(self, username: str, active: bool = True) -> None:
        self.username = username
        self.active = active


user = User("sofia")
print(user.username)
print(user.active)`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>sofia
True</pre></div>
      <div class="oop-mini-example">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Čo sa stane pri User(&quot;sofia&quot;)?" en="What happens in User(&quot;sofia&quot;)?" /></strong>
        <ol>
          <li><LocalizedText sk="Python vytvorí novú inštanciu User." en="Python creates a new User instance." /></li>
          <li><LocalizedText sk="Automaticky zavolá __init__ a odovzdá jej self a username." en="It automatically calls __init__ and passes self and username." /></li>
          <li><LocalizedText sk="Atribúty username a active dostanú počiatočné hodnoty." en="The username and active attributes receive their initial values." /></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="self pri vytváraní objektu nepíšeš ručne. Volanie user = User(&quot;sofia&quot;) ho odovzdá automaticky. __init__ nevracia nový objekt — jeho úlohou je inicializácia." en="You do not pass self manually when creating an object. The call user = User(&quot;sofia&quot;) supplies it automatically. __init__ does not return a new object — its job is initialization." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="attributes">
      <h2>4. <LocalizedText sk="Atribúty: údaje inštancie a triedy" en="Attributes: instance and class data" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Atribút je pomenovaná hodnota priradená objektu alebo triede. Atribúty inštancie sa zvyčajne nastavujú cez self v __init__ a každý objekt má svoje vlastné hodnoty. Atribút triedy je definovaný priamo v tele triedy a je spoločný, pokiaľ ho inštancia neprekryje vlastnou hodnotou." en="An attribute is a named value attached to an object or class. Instance attributes are usually assigned through self in __init__, and each object has its own values. A class attribute is defined in the class body and is shared unless an instance shadows it with its own value." /></p>
      <div class="oop-comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="oop-comparison-table">
          <thead><tr><th><LocalizedText sk="Typ" en="Type" /></th><th><LocalizedText sk="Kde sa definuje" en="Where it is defined" /></th><th><LocalizedText sk="Použitie" en="Use" /></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong><LocalizedText sk="Atribút inštancie" en="Instance attribute" /></strong></td><td><code>self.name = name</code></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Vlastná hodnota každého objektu." en="A value belonging to each object." /></td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong><LocalizedText sk="Atribút triedy" en="Class attribute" /></strong></td><td><code>kind = "student"</code></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Spoločná hodnota pre triedu a jej inštancie." en="A value shared by the class and its instances." /></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Student:
    school = "TUKE"  # Class attribute

    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name  # Instance attribute


anna = Student("Anna")
peter = Student("Peter")

print(anna.name, peter.name)
print(anna.school, peter.school)`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>Anna Peter
TUKE TUKE</pre></div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Pozor na meniteľné atribúty triedy. Zoznam definovaný ako members = [] v tele triedy by zdieľali všetky inštancie. Ak má mať každý študent vlastný zoznam, vytvor ho v __init__ ako self.members = []." en="Be careful with mutable class attributes. A list defined as members = [] in the class body would be shared by all instances. If every student needs a separate list, create it in __init__ as self.members = []." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="methods">
      <h2>5. <LocalizedText sk="Metódy: operácie nad objektom" en="Methods: operations on an object" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Metóda je funkcia definovaná v triede. Bežná inštančná metóda má ako prvý parameter self, takže môže čítať alebo meniť atribúty konkrétneho objektu. Metódy pomáhajú sústrediť pravidlá práce s údajmi na jedno miesto." en="A method is a function defined in a class. A regular instance method takes self as its first parameter, so it can read or change the attributes of a particular object. Methods keep the rules for working with data in one place." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Counter:
    def __init__(self, start: int = 0) -> None:
        self.value = start

    def increment(self) -> None:
        self.value += 1

    def reset(self) -> None:
        self.value = 0

    def current_value(self) -> int:
        return self.value


counter = Counter(4)
counter.increment()
counter.increment()
print(counter.current_value())
counter.reset()
print(counter.current_value())`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>6
0</pre></div>
      <div class="oop-mini-example">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Rozdiel medzi volaním metódy a funkcie" en="Calling a method vs. a function" /></strong>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="counter.increment() je volanie metódy na konkrétnom objekte. Metóda dostane objekt automaticky ako self." en="counter.increment() calls a method on a specific object. The method receives the object automatically as self." /></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="interaction">
      <h2>6. <LocalizedText sk="Interakcia objektov" en="Object interaction" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="V reálnom programe objekty zvyčajne nepracujú samostatne. Jeden objekt môže zavolať metódu druhého objektu a odovzdať mu údaje. Takto sa zodpovednosti rozdelia medzi menšie časti programu." en="In a real program, objects usually do not work alone. One object can call another object's method and pass it data. This divides responsibilities between smaller parts of a program." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Student:
    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name


class Course:
    def __init__(self, title: str) -> None:
        self.title = title
        self.students: list[Student] = []

    def enroll(self, student: Student) -> None:
        self.students.append(student)

    def print_students(self) -> None:
        for student in self.students:
            print(student.name)


python_course = Course("Python")
python_course.enroll(Student("Anna"))
python_course.enroll(Student("Peter"))
python_course.print_students()`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>Anna
Peter</pre></div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Course nepozná vnútorné detaily vytvárania študenta. Dostane hotový objekt Student a používa jeho verejné rozhranie. To znižuje previaznutosť medzi triedami." en="Course does not need to know the internal details of creating a student. It receives a Student object and uses its public interface. This reduces coupling between classes." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="inheritance">
      <h2>7. <LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť, prepisovanie metód a super()" en="Inheritance, method overriding and super()" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť vyjadruje vzťah „je typom“ (is-a). Podtrieda preberá dostupné atribúty a metódy rodičovskej triedy a môže pridať vlastné. Použi ju vtedy, keď podtrieda naozaj predstavuje špecializovaný typ rodičovskej triedy." en="Inheritance represents an “is-a” relationship. A subclass inherits accessible attributes and methods from its parent class and can add its own. Use it when the subclass genuinely represents a specialized type of the parent class." /></p>
      <div class="oop-diagram oop-diagram-vertical" role="group" aria-label="Inheritance relationship">
        <div class="oop-diagram-node"><strong>Person</strong><span>name</span><span>introduce()</span></div>
        <div class="oop-diagram-connector"><span>↑ <LocalizedText sk="dedičnosť" en="inherits" /> ↑</span></div>
        <div class="oop-diagram-node"><strong>Student</strong><span>student_id</span><span>introduce() — override</span></div>
      </div>
      <h3><LocalizedText sk="Prepisovanie (overriding)" en="Method overriding" /></h3>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Podtrieda môže definovať metódu s rovnakým názvom ako rodičovská trieda. Pri volaní na objekte podtriedy sa použije nová implementácia. Takto podtrieda prispôsobí zdedené správanie." en="A subclass can define a method with the same name as one in the parent class. When called on a subclass instance, the new implementation is used. This lets the subclass customize inherited behavior." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Person:
    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name

    def introduce(self) -> str:
        return f"My name is {self.name}."


class Student(Person):
    def introduce(self) -> str:
        return f"I'm {self.name}, a student."


person = Person("Eva")
student = Student("Anna")
print(person.introduce())
print(student.introduce())`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>My name is Eva.
I'm Anna, a student.</pre></div>
      <h3><code>super()</code></h3>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="super() umožňuje zavolať ďalšiu implementáciu metódy podľa poradia vyhľadávania metód (MRO). V jednoduchom príklade dedičnosti tým zavoláš implementáciu rodičovskej triedy. Je užitočné najmä pri rozšírení inicializácie alebo správania bez kopírovania kódu." en="super() lets you call the next implementation of a method according to the method resolution order (MRO). In a simple inheritance example, this calls the parent class implementation. It is especially useful when extending initialization or behavior without copying code." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Person:
    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name

    def describe(self) -> str:
        return f"Name: {self.name}"


class Student(Person):
    def __init__(self, name: str, student_id: str) -> None:
        super().__init__(name)
        self.student_id = student_id

    def describe(self) -> str:
        parent_text = super().describe()
        return f"{parent_text}, ID: {self.student_id}"


student = Student("Anna", "B123")
print(student.describe())`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>Name: Anna, ID: B123</pre></div>
      <div class="oop-mini-example">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Zapamätaj si" en="Remember" /></strong>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Overriding mení alebo rozširuje zdedenú metódu. super() umožňuje nadviazať na ďalšiu implementáciu namiesto toho, aby si celý pôvodný kód kopíroval." en="Overriding changes or extends an inherited method. super() lets you build on the next implementation instead of copying all the original code." /></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="composition">
      <h2>8. <LocalizedText sk="Kompozícia: vzťah has-a" en="Composition: the has-a relationship" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Kompozícia vyjadruje vzťah „má“ (has-a). Objekt obsahuje alebo používa iný objekt ako svoju súčasť. Na rozdiel od dedičnosti nejde o špecializovaný typ — napríklad kurz má študentov, ale kurz nie je študent." en="Composition represents a “has-a” relationship. An object contains or uses another object as one of its parts. Unlike inheritance, this is not a specialized type — for example, a course has students, but a course is not a student." /></p>
      <div class="oop-diagram" role="group" aria-label="Composition relationship">
        <div class="oop-diagram-node"><strong>Course</strong><span>title</span><span>enroll()</span></div>
        <div class="oop-diagram-connector"><span>◇ <LocalizedText sk="má" en="has" /> ◇</span></div>
        <div class="oop-diagram-node"><strong>Student</strong><span>name</span><span>student_id</span></div>
      </div>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Student:
    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name


class Course:
    def __init__(self, title: str) -> None:
        self.title = title
        self.students: list[Student] = []

    def enroll(self, student: Student) -> None:
        self.students.append(student)

    def student_names(self) -> list[str]:
        return [student.name for student in self.students]


course = Course("Python Basics")
course.enroll(Student("Anna"))
course.enroll(Student("Peter"))
print(course.student_names())`} />
      <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong><pre>['Anna', 'Peter']</pre></div>
      <div class="oop-comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="oop-comparison-table">
          <thead><tr><th><LocalizedText sk="Otázka" en="Question" /></th><th><LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť — is-a" en="Inheritance — is-a" /></th><th><LocalizedText sk="Kompozícia — has-a" en="Composition — has-a" /></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><LocalizedText sk="Vzťah" en="Relationship" /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Student je Person." en="A Student is a Person." /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Course má Student objekty." en="A Course has Student objects." /></td></tr>
            <tr><td><LocalizedText sk="Účel" en="Purpose" /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Špecializovať existujúci typ." en="Specialize an existing type." /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Spojiť objekty s rôznymi zodpovednosťami." en="Connect objects with different responsibilities." /></td></tr>
            <tr><td><LocalizedText sk="Kedy zvoliť" en="When to choose" /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Keď podtrieda môže zastúpiť rodičovskú triedu." en="When the subclass can stand in for the parent class." /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Keď objekt potrebuje služby alebo údaje iného objektu." en="When an object needs the services or data of another object." /></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Praktické pravidlo: ak vieš prirodzene povedať „A je B“, zváž dedičnosť. Ak vieš povedať „A má B“ alebo „A používa B“, zvyčajne je vhodnejšia kompozícia." en="Practical rule: if you can naturally say “A is a B”, consider inheritance. If you can say “A has a B” or “A uses a B”, composition is usually a better fit." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="design-mistakes">
      <h2>9. <LocalizedText sk="Typické chyby návrhu tried" en="Common class design mistakes" /></h2>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="1. Príliš veľká trieda" en="1. A class with too many responsibilities" /></h3>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Trieda, ktorá načítava súbory, počíta výsledky, formátuje report a zobrazuje používateľské rozhranie, má priveľa zodpovedností. Rozdeľ ju na menšie triedy alebo funkcie, z ktorých každá rieši jasnú úlohu." en="A class that reads files, calculates results, formats reports and displays the user interface has too many responsibilities. Split it into smaller classes or functions, each with a clear job." /></p>
      </div>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="2. Dedičnosť použitá iba na zdieľanie kódu" en="2. Inheritance used only to share code" /></h3>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Nevytváraj podtriedu, ak medzi typmi neexistuje skutočný vzťah is-a. Ak objekt iba potrebuje použiť inú službu, odovzdaj mu ju ako atribút — použi kompozíciu." en="Do not create a subclass if there is no genuine is-a relationship. If an object only needs to use another service, pass it in as an attribute — use composition." /></p>
      </div>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="3. Zdieľaný meniteľný atribút triedy" en="3. Shared mutable class attribute" /></h3>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Zoznam alebo slovník definovaný priamo v triede zdieľajú všetky inštancie. Ak má byť hodnota nezávislá pre každý objekt, inicializuj ju v __init__." en="A list or dictionary defined directly in the class is shared by all instances. If the value should be independent for each object, initialize it in __init__." /></p>
        <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Team:
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self.members: list[str] = []  # Separate list per instance`} />
      </div>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="4. Zabudnuté volanie super().__init__()" en="4. Forgetting super().__init__()" /></h3>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Ak rodičovská trieda inicializuje atribúty potrebné pre všetky jej podtriedy, nezabudni pri rozšírení konštruktora zavolať super().__init__(...). Inak môže objekt postrádať očakávané údaje." en="If the parent class initializes attributes needed by all its subclasses, remember to call super().__init__(...) when extending the initializer. Otherwise, the object may be missing expected data." /></p>
      </div>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="5. Zbytočné metódy a nejasné názvy" en="5. Unnecessary methods and unclear names" /></h3>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Metódy pomenuj podľa toho, čo robia, napríklad calculate_total() alebo enroll(). Nevytváraj metódu pre každé jednoduché čítanie atribútu, ak nepridáva žiadne pravidlo ani správanie." en="Name methods after what they do, such as calculate_total() or enroll(). Do not create a method for every simple attribute read if it adds no rule or behavior." /></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="practice">
      <h2>10. <LocalizedText sk="Praktické precvičenie" en="Practice task" /></h2>
      <div class="oop-task-card">
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Vytvor triedu Book s atribútmi title, author a pages. Pridaj metódu summary(), ktorá vráti opis knihy, a metódu is_long(), ktorá vráti True, ak má kniha aspoň 300 strán. Vytvor dva objekty a vypíš ich opisy aj výsledok is_long()." en="Create a Book class with title, author and pages attributes. Add a summary() method that returns a description of the book and an is_long() method that returns True if the book has at least 300 pages. Create two objects and print their summaries and is_long() results." /></p>
        <p><strong><LocalizedText sk="Najprv úlohu vyrieš samostatne. Potom si otvor vzorové riešenie." en="Try to solve the task yourself first. Then open the sample solution." /></strong></p>
        <details class="oop-solution">
          <summary><LocalizedText sk="Zobraziť vzorové riešenie" en="Show sample solution" /></summary>
          <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Book:
    def __init__(self, title: str, author: str, pages: int) -> None:
        if pages <= 0:
            raise ValueError("pages must be positive")
        self.title = title
        self.author = author
        self.pages = pages

    def summary(self) -> str:
        return f"{self.title} by {self.author} ({self.pages} pages)"

    def is_long(self) -> bool:
        return self.pages >= 300


book_a = Book("Clean Code", "Robert C. Martin", 464)
book_b = Book("Small Python Guide", "A. Novak", 120)
print(book_a.summary())
print(book_a.is_long())
print(book_b.summary())
print(book_b.is_long())`} />
          <div class="oop-output"><strong><LocalizedText sk="Očakávaný výstup" en="Expected output" /></strong><pre>Clean Code by Robert C. Martin (464 pages)
True
Small Python Guide by A. Novak (120 pages)
False</pre></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section oop-self-check" id="self-check">
      <h2><LocalizedText sk="Rýchla kontrola porozumenia" en="Quick self-check" /></h2>
      <details>
        <summary><LocalizedText sk="1. Aký je rozdiel medzi triedou a objektom?" en="1. What is the difference between a class and an object?" /></summary>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Trieda je definícia typu; objekt je konkrétna inštancia tejto triedy." en="A class defines a type; an object is a particular instance of that class." /></p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><LocalizedText sk="2. Čo je stav objektu a čo jeho správanie?" en="2. What are an object's state and behavior?" /></summary>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Stav tvoria hodnoty atribútov; správanie tvoria metódy, ktoré s týmito údajmi pracujú." en="State consists of attribute values; behavior consists of methods that work with that data." /></p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><LocalizedText sk="3. Čo znamená is-a a has-a?" en="3. What do is-a and has-a mean?" /></summary>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Is-a opisuje dedičnosť (Student je Person). Has-a opisuje kompozíciu (Course má Student objekty)." en="Is-a describes inheritance (a Student is a Person). Has-a describes composition (a Course has Student objects)." /></p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><LocalizedText sk="4. Na čo slúži super()?" en="4. What is super() used for?" /></summary>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Umožňuje zavolať ďalšiu implementáciu metódy v poradí MRO, často rodičovskú implementáciu v jednoduchej dedičnosti." en="It calls the next method implementation in the MRO, often the parent implementation in simple inheritance." /></p>
      </details>
    </section>

